# Streamclone Pulse & StreamPulse

Cursor-specific guardrails. Generic routing stays in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

## Read docs before code

Before changing extension, portal, coverage, backfill, or hosted API behavior, read:

- [`docs/pulse-extension/live-coverage-requirements.md`](../../docs/pulse-extension/live-coverage-requirements.md)
- [`docs/website-portal/design.md`](../../docs/website-portal/design.md)
- [`docs/website-portal/tasks.md`](../../docs/website-portal/tasks.md)

Backend changes → sibling **streamclone** checkout (`../twitch-7tv-clone`); implement Go APIs there, not in this repo.

## Guardrails (non-negotiable)

- No unauthenticated `/watch`
- No raw chat exposed to extension or portal
- No client-side Pulse scoring
- No fake progress (coverage/backfill UI must match backend state)
- No full timeline fetch on live polling
- Backend coverage, peaks, sync, and backfill states are source of truth
- D1 is user state only — never rollups, raw chat, VOD chat, TwitchTracker, or corpus data

## Cursor surfaces (this repo)

| Surface | Path | Use |
|---------|------|-----|
| Rules | `.cursor/rules/` | Always-on Cursor behavior |
| Skills | `.cursor/skills/` | Reusable workflows (`coverage-triage`, `streamclone-task-runner`, …) |
| Subagents | `.cursor/agents/` | Three reviewers only — do not spawn a swarm |
| Hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` | Lightweight lint/format/secret guards |

Default backend: `http://localhost:8090` (Caddy in streamclone). Content scripts: `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` only — no `fetch`.
